Cache: SDD

Purpose:
  Cache technology catalog with comparison criteria, selection rules,
  and integration patterns. Root stack/ defines reusable cache knowledge;
  instances/vkard.az/stack/ stores the selected cache for the project.

Catalog:
  Redis:
    Type: In-memory Key-Value
    Pros:
      - Sub-millisecond latency
      - Rich data structures
      - Pub/Sub
      - Lua scripting
      - Persistence options
    Cons:
      - Memory-limited
      - Not a primary store
    BestFor:
      - Application cache
      - Session storage
      - Rate limiting
      - Leaderboards
      - Real-time features
    AvoidWhen:
      - Large datasets
      - Primary data store
    Integration:
      - Direct client libraries
      - Spring Cache abstraction
      - Laravel Cache
    Patterns:
      - Cache-aside
      - Write-through
      - Write-behind
      - Refresh-ahead

  Valkey:
    Type: In-memory Key-Value
    Pros:
      - Open source fork
      - API compatible with Redis
      - Community-driven
    Cons:
      - Newer (less mature)
      - Smaller ecosystem
    BestFor:
      - Redis alternative
      - Open source preference
    AvoidWhen:
      - Production-critical without review

  Memcached:
    Type: In-memory Key-Value
    Pros:
      - Simple
      - Multi-threaded
      - Low memory overhead
    Cons:
      - Limited data types
      - No persistence
      - No pub/sub
    BestFor:
      - Simple caching
      - Session storage
    AvoidWhen:
      - Complex caching needs

  Varnish:
    Type: HTTP Cache
    Pros:
      - High-performance HTTP cache
      - VCL configuration
      - Load balancing
    Cons:
      - HTTP only
      - Complex configuration
    BestFor:
      - CDN edge cache
      - API response caching
    AvoidWhen:
      - Application-level cache

SelectionRules:
  - Latency: required response time
  - DataSize: cache dataset size
  - Structure: need for complex data types
  - Persistence: durability requirements
  - Consistency: cache invalidation strategy
  - Integration: compatibility with existing stack

TechnologyScore:
  Latency: 0-25
  DataSize: 0-20
  Structure: 0-15
  Persistence: 0-10
  Consistency: 0-10
  Integration: 0-20

State: +
  